<title>UK: BOE invites band 1,2 bills, shortage 700 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BOE invites band 1,2 bills, shortage 700 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England invited a round of fixed rate operations, comprising repos to March 18 and outright bills maturing on or before  March 18.</p>
<p>The Bank's repo rate is 6.0 percent.</p>
<p>It revised its forecast for the money market shortage to 700 million stg from the initial estimate of 600 million.</p>
</text>
